----------------
New Features / Enhancements
----------------
* Added gcc 5.2 which is now the default compiler (gcc 4.8 and 4.9 are
also provided)
* Updated linux-yocto kernel for qemu* and reference BSPs to version 4.1
* Added basic support for Altera Nios II and Adapteva Epiphany
* Added tune files for Cavium ThunderX, Cavium Octeon, ARM Cortex-A17,
Intel Quark X1000, and ARM vfpv3 and vfpv3d16 features
* Added support for building baremetal toolchains
* Added support for building nativesdk versions of the toolchain, to
potentially replace the host toolchain
* Added recipes to the core: iw, alsa-plugins, ruby, iso-codes, libcap-ng,
p11-kit, libwnck3, libwebp, libsecret, libyaml, swig, gcr, gnome-desktop3,
gsettings-desktop-schemas. Many of these were added in order to be able to
build the most recent version of webkitgtk and epiphany, which have also
been added.
* Added support for GPG-signed RPM packages and package feeds
* Added basic support for sstate package signing/validation
* Stale files from removed/renamed recipes now automatically removed from
the sysroot
* bitbake variable overrides now handled dynamically (update_data() no
longer required)
* Toaster Web UI improvements:
  - Improved performance and reliability: Toaster now builds almost
anything you throw at it
  - Simplified setup process: get Toaster up and running with a single
command
  - Support for Z shell (zsh)
  - New project UI with better navigation and layout
  - Improved layer dependency handling: Toaster will now retrieve and
display second-level layer dependencies
  - Separate list of image recipes: available images are now easier to
find and build
* wic image creation tool version 0.2.0, including bug fixes, code cleanup
and new features:
  - fixed support for GPT partition tables
  - uses native tools (parted, mkfs, mtools, etc)
  - add image compression support
  - add partition UUID support
  - add plugin for hybrid iso image
  - add plugin for single partition disk
  - add support for building rootfs externally (wic invokes bitbake to
build the image)
  - support ontrackdm6aux3 partitions for Freescale mxs platforms
* Image generation improvements:
  - Added qcow2 type
  - Added vdi (VirtualBox VDI) type
  - Added hdddirect type
  - Added wic image type (invokes wic)
  - Support specifying and initramfs for VM image formats
  - Added a mechanism for creating a companion debug filesystem
* Added support for partition UUIDs in a number of places
* Initramfs (initramfs-framework) improvements:
  - Support dropping into shell on failure
  - Added boot parameters: init, ro, rootflags, rootfstype
* runqemu: added support for full-disk images
* mkefidisk: added interactive menu
* kernel: added basic fitImage support
* devtool improvements:
  - update-recipe: add option to write changes to bbappend
  - update-recipe: avoid updating patches that have not been modified
  - update-recipe: 'auto' mode now defaults to 'patch' mode for git
recipes unless commits pushed upstream
  - add: set up fetched source as a git repository by default
  - add: add an option to fetch source from a remote URL
  - add: handle binary-only packages
  - modify: improved support for kernel recipes
  - build: allow disabling make parallelism
  - New "upgrade" subcommand for upgrading a recipe
  - Added handling for local files within recipe
  - Fixed handling of separate build and source directories
* recipetool improvements:
  - Added "newappend" sub-command to create a blank bbappend file
  - Added "appendfile" subcommand to create a bbappend to replace a file
on the target
  - Added "appendsrcfile(s)" subcommands to create a bbappend to replace
source file(s) in a recipe
* Extensible SDK now in beta state; many bugfixes and improvements
including:
  - Added ability to build images and packages
  - Added "devtool search" command for recipe keyword search
  - Added ability to run QEMU
  - Added extensible SDK update mechanism
* runqemu: enable support for kvm without vhost for x86 and x86_64
* Added ability for devtool, recipetool and oe-selftest to be extended
from other layers
* buildhistory: now creates files-in-package.txt listing files, sizes and
permissions per package
* buildhistory: added metadata revisions and build result to commit message
* archiver.bbclass: Allow filtering recipes by name for source archiving
* packagegroup-base: pull in iw as well as wireless-tools for more modern
wireless device configuration
* bitbake: allow ~ in bblayers.conf
* bitbake: fetch2: added BB_ALLOWED_NETWORKS support
* bitbake: fetch2: support submodules in hg fetcher
* bitbake: added BB_TASK_IONICE_LEVEL to set ionice for tasks
* bitbake: datastore now injected into event handlers as 'd'
* bitbake-layers: show-recipes: added -i option to filter by class
inheritance
* COMBINED_FEATURES is now programmatically generated from
MACHINE_FEATURES / DISTRO_FEATURES instead of being a hardcoded subset
* Shell message functions (bbplain, bbwarn, bberror, bbfatal) now output
through the bitbake UI like their python counterparts
* Improved support for building with musl libc (musl itself is still
external, in meta-musl)
* Enabled virtio support for qemu* machines for better I/O performance
* Added pbzip2, now used to compress images and SDKs when using bzip2
compression
* Added ptest support to nettle, qemu, libevent, e2fsprogs, mdadm, rt-tests
* Added x11 to REQUIRED_DISTRO_FEATURES for recipes that cannot be built
without x11
* Made sstate checksums of native and target stay the same between 32 and
64-bit build hosts, or when SDKMACHINE changes, and added tests to ensure
this doesn't regress
* Made sstate checksums of target stay the same when name (but not
substance) of machine changes, and added tests to ensure this doesn't
regress
* Binaries staged into the sysroot are now stripped of debugging symbols
in order to save space
* Parallelised sstate mirror checks and print status note
* Use immediate expansion for os.uname() in bitbake.conf for a 2% parsing
speedup
* Backwards compatibility with the Yocto Project Community Manager 1.9
"jefro" release
* Reimplemented license manifest creation in python
* Changed gnome recipe tarball compression to xz
* tune-core2.inc: set X86ARCH32 to i686 (instead of i586)
* kern-tools: optimized kernel patching performance
* Improved SDK extraction time by 10-50%

